  "description": "The three Squib types the user can choose. The class is a strict one-design: every builder used the same hull form and sail plan (C10), so the types differ only where the sources say they do - the cockpit (self-draining since Rondar, C9, C10) and the sails (the new Hyde B3 / Batt designs, C11, C12) - plus estimates (E) labelled as such. Each type is a hull build plus a sail package; 'calibration' holds partial calibration.json documents merged over the defaults.",
  "updated": "2026-10-25"
 },
